  "name": "steam-spring",
  "vibe": "Slate #33404a walls, cedar #a8794a, and a pale aqua #7fc4bd that only ever means water. Castoro's bookish serif sets two-line titles that fade up on an unusually soft entrance — drowse — while Catamaran handles the small print. Behind them the pack draws an actual hot spring: an aqua pool ellipse ringed with ink boulders, ripple rings widening across its surface, three fat steam curls climbing and thinning out of frame, pale flecks drifting down, and a wooden post whose paper lantern breathes amber. The camera never hurries — rotation 0.3, a long 30% settle, no spin move anywhere. Its signature beat is hand-lettering: a guest-book entry arrives one rotated word at a time, every fourth word in aqua. For onsen, spa, sauna, retreat and slow hospitality.",
